<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n53175" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καπν-ίας</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>, ὁ, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καπνός</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>smoky</i>, nickname of the Comic
			poet Ecphantides, Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>V.</u>
				151
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> as
				Subst., </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>1.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ. οἶνος, ὁ</span>, expl. by <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phot.
			</span></i> as wine <i>that had a smoky taste</i> from having been
			long hung up in smoke, <i><span class="en">
				Pherecr.
				130.6
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Anaxandr.
				41.71
			</span></i> (anap.), <i><span class="en">
				Pl.Com.
				244
			</span></i>: perh. rather to be expld. as <i>made from the vine</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάπνειος</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κ</span>. (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λίθος</span>), ὁ, a kind of
			<i>jasper</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				5.142
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plin.
				<u>HN</u>
				37.118
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
